{"type":"text","timestamp":1785364600980,"sessionID":"ses_0500256c3ffeNYTAeI7P8igMgY","part":{"id":"prt_fb005ce53001r6NIRYLcg0joyF","messageID":"msg_fb005cab9001JNMYLoldxfv1Js","sessionID":"ses_0500256c3ffeNYTAeI7P8igMgY","type":"text","text":"I've created a Notion-like workspace application with:\n\n**Files created:**\n- `/workspace/app.py` - Python Flask backend with SQLite database\n- `/workspace/start.sh` - Startup script that handles dependencies and runs the app\n- `/workspace/pyproject.toml` - Project configuration for uv\n\n**Features implemented:**\n- Create, edit, and delete text blocks via REST API\n- Intuitive web UI with toolbar buttons (+ New Block, Delete Selected)\n- Keyboard navigation (Enter/Space to select block, Ctrl+Delete to delete)\n- Data persists across server restarts using SQLite\n- Accessible keyboard controls for all operations\n\n**To start the app:**\n```bash\nPORT=8765 sh start.sh\n```\n\nThe application will:\n1. Install dependencies via uv\n2. Initialize SQLite database with default block\n3. Run Flask server on PORT 8765 (or custom port)\n4. Keep running in foreground, preserving data across invocations","time":{"start":1785364598355,"end":1785364600962}}}
